SRR23002308	PRJNA791926	SRP352300	SAMN32620271	SRX18958118	Mus musculus	RRBS_ESCs_siRNA_Dnmt1_rep2	RRBS_ESCs_siRNA_Dnmt1_rep2	Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM6921493: RRBS_ESCs_siRNA_Dnmt1_rep2 Mus musculus Bisulfite-Seq	Bisulfite-Seq	GENOMIC	Reduced Representation	PAIRED	ILLUMINA	Illumina HiSeq 4000	DNA samples were extracted using the NucleoSpin RNA purification kit and NucleoSpin RNA/DNA Buffer Set for parallel RNA and DNA purification (Macherey-Nagel) according to the manufacturer's instructions. RRBS libraries were prepared as described in Bender et al. (2021), Methods Mol Biol 2214:207-220. Briefly, 100 ng genomic DNA were digested with MspI (Thermo Fisher Scientific), end-repaired and A-tailed with Klenow fragment exo- (Thermo Fisher Scientific) and ligated to methylated adapters with T4 DNA ligase (Thermo Fisher Scientific) in Tango 1X buffer. DNA fragments ranging from 150 to 400 bp were selected by gel excision, purified using the MinElute gel extraction kit (Qiagen) and bisulfite-converted twice with the EpiTect bisulfite kit (Qiagen). The libraries were amplified using the Pfu Turbo Cx hotstart DNA polymerase (Agilent) with 12 PCR cycles and purified using Agencourt AmpureXP beads (Beckman-Coulter).	40576675	8115335000	ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR230/008/SRR23002308/SRR23002308_1.fastq.gz;ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR230/008/SRR23002308/SRR23002308_2.fastq.gz	9608cd8d20467edc9c61348ce1e7a72c;ade52f655db792a661bb46744ba6e372	1728883639;1612073574
